641
00:10:21,650 --> 00:10:22,530
And then...

642
00:10:22,530 --> 00:10:24,620
You ran over to Phone Microwave-chan

643
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:26,280
and started panting...

644
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:29,080
Mayushii, can you say "panting" again?

645
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:30,620
Stop it, pervert!

646
00:10:42,010 --> 00:10:42,510
Buy Lotto-6

647
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:43,470
It's here.

648
00:10:42,510 --> 00:10:43,470
You'll win!

649
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:47,970
Okabe... Are you really all right?

650
00:10:47,970 --> 00:10:49,060
Where's the money?

651
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:50,140
The Lotto-6!

652
00:10:50,490 --> 00:10:52,850
Cel-7, did I win third prize?

653
00:10:52,850 --> 00:10:54,440
Don't call me Cel-7...

654
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:56,610
What are you talking about?

655
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:59,440
What do you mean? You...

656
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:00,690
Okarin?

657
00:11:01,690 --> 00:11:03,030
The experiment?

658
00:11:03,030 --> 00:11:05,820
We did an experiment to see if we could change the past with the D-mail...

659
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:08,740
We were just talking about what we could

660
00:11:08,740 --> 00:11:10,410
do for the experiment.

661
00:11:11,290 --> 00:11:15,170
Mayushii wants something that will bring about world peace!

662
00:11:15,170 --> 00:11:18,960
Like giving everyone in the world an Upa cushion!

663
00:11:16,210 --> 00:11:18,960
You really don't remember...

664
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:24,220
Come in!

665
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:28,220
It's Ruka-kun!

666
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:29,560
Welcome!

667
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:35,440
Kyouma-san, I'm sorry!

668
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:36,400
Ruka-kun?

669
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:37,940
This...

670
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:42,400
02, 12, 18...

671
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:43,900
It's the same.

672
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:46,610
Rukako! Where did you get this?

673
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:51,080
Um... You gave me the numbers.

674
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:51,910
I did?

675
00:11:52,250 --> 00:11:55,660
You said to buy it since it might win.

676
00:11:55,660 --> 00:11:57,290
Wh-When?

677
00:11:57,290 --> 00:11:58,960
One week ago.

678
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:01,840
Wow, Okarin's psychic!

679
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:04,420
So, Ruka, did you win?

680
00:12:04,420 --> 00:12:08,340
Well... I got one of the numbers wrong.

681
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:14,140
So close!

682
00:12:14,470 --> 00:12:15,560
Too close!

683
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:19,440
Okabe, did you use the Phone Microwave to...

684
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:24,740
<i>Hey, there's no Dr Pepper!</i>

685
00:12:24,990 --> 00:12:25,780
<i>They didn't have any.</i>

686
00:12:25,780 --> 00:12:27,320
<i>What do you want me to do about it?</i>

687
00:12:35,830 --> 00:12:38,420
<i>I sent the D-mail.</i>

688
00:12:38,870 --> 00:12:41,340
<i>But there's no record of it.</i>

689
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:45,550
<i>The past has been changed?</i>

690
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:48,930
<i>They didn't remember the experiment,</i>

691
00:12:49,890 --> 00:12:52,600
<i>even though we all talked about it, and we all observed.</i>

692
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:55,350
<i>Only I remember.</i>

693
00:12:56,210 --> 00:12:57,600
<i>Only I...</i>

694
00:12:58,850 --> 00:13:01,150
<i>This feeling! It's just like back then...</i>

695
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,360
<i>What is this?</i>

696
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,490
What's that?

697
00:13:17,650 --> 00:13:18,830
Something important.

698
00:13:26,630 --> 00:13:27,550
What's wrong?

699
00:13:29,930 --> 00:13:32,300
You look like you've been brainwashed.

700
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:34,050
Brainwashed...

701
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:36,890
It's possible.

702
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:40,850
But was I the one brainwashed... Or were they?

703
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:42,150
What?

704
00:13:52,910 --> 00:13:54,200
There's no chip.

705
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,490
It's okay.

706
00:13:56,490 --> 00:13:58,160
You're not brainwashed.

707
00:13:58,160 --> 00:13:59,370
Chip?

708
00:14:00,330 --> 00:14:02,120
What's brainwashed?

709
00:14:02,810 --> 00:14:04,130
That's...

710
00:14:04,630 --> 00:14:08,210
I, Hououin Kyouma, will tell you.

711
00:14:09,010 --> 00:14:12,260
I guess Nae's scared of Okabe Rintarou.

712
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:15,930
There's something I want to ask you.

713
00:14:20,810 --> 00:14:21,940
Electricity?

714
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:23,560
You mean when there are all those sparks?

715
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:25,400
You did it before, didn't you?

716
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:27,650
There should have been one ten minutes ago.

717
00:14:27,650 --> 00:14:29,740
I didn't notice that one.

718
00:14:30,030 --> 00:14:30,820
What about you, Nae?

719
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:31,900
Nope!

720
00:14:33,660 --> 00:14:35,700
You really are a pervert!

721
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:37,330
I'm not a pervert!

722
00:14:37,330 --> 00:14:39,200
I'm a pervert gentleman!

723
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:40,290
See?

724
00:14:40,290 --> 00:14:42,330
I told you that you can hear it.

725
00:14:42,330 --> 00:14:43,750
I didn't know it was this bad...

726
00:14:44,710 --> 00:14:47,130
Did you hear about the time machine?

727
00:14:47,540 --> 00:14:49,880
Yeah. Nice job, I guess!

728
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:51,380
Let me warn you...

729
00:14:51,380 --> 00:14:53,970
I won't tell anyone.

730
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:58,430
Are you worried about something related to the time machine?

731
00:14:59,180 --> 00:15:02,270
Then why not ask John Titor?

732
00:15:04,350 --> 00:15:08,520
<i>Come to think of it, John Titor mentioned this.</i>

733
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:10,900
<i>If you go to the past and change it,</i>

734
00:15:10,900 --> 00:15:13,900
<i>this alters something called the divergence number,</i>

735
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:16,490
<i>and the world line moves to another world.</i>

736
00:15:17,370 --> 00:15:23,210
<i>When there's a world line move, 
people's memories are altered.</i>

737
00:15:23,210 --> 00:15:26,880
<i>And memories of the new world are created.</i>

738
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:29,000
<i>The D-mail moved the world line</i>

739
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:32,010
<i>from a world where Rukako didn't buy the Lotto-6 ticket</i>

740
00:15:32,010 --> 00:15:33,630
<i>to one where he did.</i>

741
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:39,010
<i>The world line changed, and so did the past.</i>

742
00:15:39,010 --> 00:15:40,140
<i>In this world,</i>

743
00:15:40,140 --> 00:15:42,430
<i>I didn't send the D-mailwith the winning Loto 6 number</i>

744
00:15:42,430 --> 00:15:44,060
<i>into the past.</i>

745
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:47,560
<i>It's not that the other Lab Members don't remember the experiment.</i>

